    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d514">

                <pb facs="0701" n="601" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg601"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">211.65/99: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Italy</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-10T13:00:00-05:00">March 10, 1934—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. Pointing out that present extradition treaty between United States and Italy
                    made in 1868<anchor n="15" xml:id="d514-f1"/> is not sufficiently comprehensive
                    to serve present needs of two Governments, please inquire of Foreign Office
                    whether Italian Government will agree to negotiate new extradition treaty with
                    United States and if so whether it will instruct its Ambassador to this country
                    to take up the matter promptly with the Department.</p>
                <p>It is desired if practicable to submit this treaty to the Senate before end
                    present session.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
